  "evidence_notes": "Lisa, 31, diagnosed with Crohn's 5 years ago. Also has endometriosis and migraines. Symptoms initially dismissed. Started mesalamine and brief prednisone, then azathioprine which caused pancreatitis. Moved to biologics: Remicade (inconvenient infusions), then Humira (home injections). Stable on Humira for 2 years, but experiences mini-flares, injection anxiety, and possible Humira-induced psoriasis. Frequent upper respiratory infections. Insurance requires annual prior authorization for Humira. Managing both endometriosis and Crohn's is exhausting. Diet is restricted. Fatigue impacts work and social life. Concerned about fertility and pregnancy."
